      "value": "subject_definitions: <Picture 1> is the hero's face identity anchor. <Picture 2> is his exact charcoal hoodie and body reference. The loaded RefMod ai_everywhere_hero carries the combined identity and wardrobe references.\nsummary: A single photorealistic 5-second night-time home-studio shot for the AI Everywhere music video.\nretention_analysis: <Picture 1>: fully_preserved - retain facial identity, hair, age, and facial proportions. <Picture 2>: fully_preserved - retain the charcoal hoodie, dark trousers, and natural body build. The RefMod is fully_preserved for protagonist identity and wardrobe.\ndetailed_description: [Shot 1] Live-action cinematic footage in a modest home computer studio at 2 AM. The same young adult male creator from <Picture 1>, wearing the exact plain charcoal hoodie from <Picture 2> and no outer jacket, sits naturally at his desk facing two monitors. Blue monitor light falls across his face and hands; rain slides down the window behind him, with a distant city glow outside. He types a short sequence, pauses, and looks from the keyboard to the screen as a luminous digital cityscape blooms across one monitor. Medium over-the-shoulder three-quarter view, face clear and natural, hands anatomically plausible, monitor graphics abstract with no readable text. The camera makes one slow, small-amplitude push in. One continuous shot, no cuts, grounded domestic scale, realistic skin, cloth and glass, restrained cinematic contrast.\noverall_soundscape: Quiet room tone, soft keyboard taps, a low computer fan, and gentle rain against the window. No speech.\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A; the user's master song will be laid in during editing."
